From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: M3 Pro Linux downstream <m3pro-linux@localhost>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:02:00 -0500
Subject: [DEVELOPMENT PATCH 3/3] arm64: dts: apple: t6030: add T6030 AGX
 compatible override

Development only. Override the generic base compatible with the
SoC-specific list, as t6020.dtsi does for the M2 Pro:

  "apple,agx-t6030", "apple,agx-g15x", "apple,agx-g15s"

Each string follows from device-derived identity: chip ID 0x6030,
IOClass AGXAcceleratorG15X, and GPU generation 15 with variant S. The
middle string assumes that the existing "apple,agx-g14x" string names
the AGXAcceleratorG14X family. Nothing in this tree states that, and
t6000.dtsi uses "apple,agx-g13x" without a variant string. Upstream
naming for G15, when it exists, takes precedence.

No driver in this tree matches "apple,agx-t6030", and the pinned
apple,agx.yaml binding enumerates no G15 string. Nothing binds, and no
dt-schema pass is claimed. The node stays disabled on both J514s and
J516s.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6030.dtsi | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6030.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6030.dtsi
index 529bf0f..5ee04a5 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6030.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6030.dtsi
@@ -1535,3 +1535,12 @@
 
 #include "t6030-pmgr.dtsi"
 #include "t6030-gpu.dtsi"
+
+/*
+ * Development-only, following the t6020.dtsi pattern: SoC string from chip
+ * ID 0x6030, family string from IOClass AGXAcceleratorG15X, base string from
+ * G15 variant S. No binding or driver in this tree accepts these strings.
+ */
+&gpu {
+	compatible = "apple,agx-t6030", "apple,agx-g15x", "apple,agx-g15s";
+};
